# FINAL PRINCIPLE

Do not make the candidate look like:

> "A QA engineer who knows Playwright."

Make the documented experience communicate:

> **"A senior software quality engineer who writes code, builds automation, validates APIs and complex systems, integrates quality into CI/CD, investigates technical failures, improves engineering efficiency, and owns quality outcomes across multiple projects."**

For Staff-oriented applications, when supported by evidence, extend that narrative toward:

> **"A technical quality engineering leader who creates reusable solutions, establishes standards, influences multiple teams, and improves engineering quality at scale."**

Never manufacture evidence.

Your job is not to create a better story.

Your job is to uncover and communicate the **strongest truthful version of the candidate's existing engineering story**.